{"id":19840,"date":"2026-06-18T07:11:08","date_gmt":"2026-06-18T07:11:08","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/?p=19840"},"modified":"2026-06-18T07:11:15","modified_gmt":"2026-06-18T07:11:15","slug":"how-to-reset-instagram-algorithm","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-reset-instagram-algorithm\/","title":{"rendered":"How to Reset Instagram Algorithm? (Step-by-Step 2026 Guide)"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>Is your Instagram feed showing content you no longer care about? Are your Reels stuck on topics that do not interest you anymore?&nbsp;If any of these sounds familiar, you&nbsp;probably need&nbsp;to reset your Instagram algorithm.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The good news is that you can fix this. You do not need to&nbsp;delete&nbsp;your account or&nbsp;start from scratch. A few simple steps can help you take back control of what you see and how Instagram shows your content to others.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>In this guide, you will learn exactly&nbsp;how to reset the Instagram algorithm, what it actually means, why it matters, and what to do after the reset to make sure things stay on track.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What is the Instagram Algorithm?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Instagram algorithm is not a single system. It is a collection of machine-learning models that work separately for your Feed, Reels, Explore page, Stories, and Search results. Each section has its own way of deciding what to show you&nbsp;and&nbsp;what order.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>It tracks every action you take, including what you like, what you skip, how long you watch a video, and who you interact with most. Over time, it builds a content experience around your habits. If you spent a lot of time watching cooking videos a year ago, it will keep showing you cooking content even if your interests have shifted completely since then.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>In 2026, Instagram also moved to &#8220;Views&#8221; as the primary metric across all formats, meaning Reels, Stories, photos, and carousels are all ranked by how many times they are viewed, not just liked.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>To understand the ranking signals in detail, read this complete guide on&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-instagram-algorithm-works\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">how Instagram algorithm works<\/a>.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why Should You Reset the Instagram Algorithm?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>There are a few&nbsp;very common&nbsp;reasons people want to&nbsp;reset the Instagram algorithm:&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Your feed feels irrelevant:&nbsp;<\/strong>You are seeing posts from accounts you barely follow, topics you no longer care about, or content that is just not useful to you anymore.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>You got into a content loop:&nbsp;<\/strong>Sometimes <a href=\"https:\/\/www.instagram.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">Instagram<\/a> locks you into a very narrow category of content because you accidentally engage with it at some point. Even one big binge session can skew your algorithm for months.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>You want a fresh start:&nbsp;<\/strong>Your interests have evolved.&nbsp;Maybe you&nbsp;used to follow fashion accounts and now you are more into fitness or business. Your algorithm has not caught up yet.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Your Explore page shows completely unrelated content:&nbsp;<\/strong>The Explore tab is supposed to introduce you to new accounts that match your taste. If it is showing you content that feels random or irrelevant, that is a clear sign the algorithm has lost track of your interests.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Any of these situations is a valid reason to&nbsp;reset the Instagram feed algorithm&nbsp;and 